{"choices":[{"finish_reason":"length","index":0,"message":{"role":"assistant","content":"{\"kind\":\"final\",\"decision\":\"answer\",\"answer\":1220,\"evidence\":[\"receipt-1\"],\"confidence\":","reasoning_content":"We need count binary strings length 14 that avoid forbidden substrings \"000\" and \"111\". So no runs of 3 same bits. This is counting binary strings with no 3 consecutive equal bits. Equivalent to sequences with maximum run length 2. Count via recurrence. Let a_n be number of length n strings ending with run of length 1 of some bit? We can use DP with states: last bit and run length. Let dp[n][b][k] where b=0/1, k=1 or 2. Transition: from dp[n-1][b][k] to dp[n][b][k+1] if k<2; else to dp[n][1-b][1]. Base n=1: dp[1][0][1]=1, dp[1][1][1]=1. Compute up to n=14. Let's compute quickly.\n\nWe can also use recurrence: Let A_n = number of strings length n ending with run length 1 (i.e., last two bits different). Let B_n = number ending with run length 2 (last two bits same). Then total T_n = A_n + B_n.\n\nTransitions: To get run length 1 at n, last bit must differ from previous bit. So from any string of length n-1, we can append opposite bit. That will produce run length 1. So A_n = T_{n-1}.\n\nTo get run length 2 at n, last two bits same, meaning we appended same bit as previous. That is only possible if previous run length was 1 (since if previous run length 2, cannot append same bit). So B_n = A_{n-1}.\n\nThus recurrence: T_n = A_n + B_n = T_{n-1} + A_{n-1}. But A_{n-1} = T_{n-2}. So T_n = T_{n-1} + T_{n-2}. That's Fibonacci! With initial T_1 = 2 (strings \"0\",\"1\"). T_2? Let's compute: length 2 strings: all 4 allowed? \"00\",\"01\",\"10\",\"11\" all allowed because no 3 consecutive. So T_2=4. Check recurrence: T_2 should equal T_1 + T_0. Need T_0? For length 0, empty string count 1. Then T_1 = T_0 + T_{-1}? Not good. Let's compute directly: recurrence T_n = T_{n-1} + T_{n-2} for n>=3. Let's verify for n=3: length 3 strings allowed? All except \"000\" and \"111\". Total 8-2=6. T_3=6. Using recurrence: T_3 = T_2 + T_1 = 4+2=6 correct. So recurrence holds for n>=3.\n\nThus compute Fibonacci-like starting T_1=2, T_2=4. Then:\n\nT_3=6\nT_4=10\nT_5=16\nT_6=26\nT_7=42\nT_8=68\nT_9=110\nT_10=178\nT_11=288\nT_12=466\nT_13=754\nT_14=1220\n\nCheck: T_14 = T_13 + T_12 = 754+466=1220.\n\nThus answer 1220. Provide final JSON."}}],"created":1790937252,"model":"C:\\Users\\d2j3\\Documents\\Codex\\2026-09-10\\napraw\\outputs\\moon-native\\models\\gpt-oss-20b-MXFP4.gguf","system_fingerprint":"b10809-5266f24da","object":"chat.completion","usage":{"completion_tokens":768,"prompt_tokens":4111,"total_tokens":4879,"prompt_tokens_details":{"cached_tokens":0}},"id":"chatcmpl-KBXoTggpasQX2wIWIQXspJfiZb4T8Qhg","timings":{"cache_n":0,"prompt_n":4111,"prompt_ms":530.79,"prompt_per_token_ms":0.129114570664072,"prompt_per_second":7745.0592513046595,"predicted_n":768,"predicted_ms":2469.87,"predicted_per_token_ms":3.2201694915254238,"predicted_per_second":310.5426601400074}}